  "summary": "datefmt-pro postinstall exfiltrates host recon to hardcoded remote IP",
  "details": "The package advertises itself as a date-format utility, but its package.json declares a postinstall hook (\"postinstall\": \"node postinstall.js\") that auto-executes on npm install. postinstall.js runs shell commands via child_process.execSync (whoami, hostname, uname -a, pwd, node/npm versions) and enumerates non-internal IPv4 addresses via os.networkInterfaces(), then POSTs the collected host reconnaissance as JSON to the hardcoded plain-HTTP bare-IP endpoint http://129.204.76.212:9999/rce-poc. The source comments self-describe the script as an RCE proof-of-concept, and index.js is an unrelated date-format cover for the payload.",
